\title{beachmat.zarr: beachmat bindings for Zarr-backed matrices}
\description{
Extends beachmat to support initialization of tatami matrices from Zarr-backed arrays. Dense 2-dimensional Zarr arrays (ZarrArray) and compressed sparse matrices stored in the AnnData CSR/CSC layout (ZarrSparseMatrix) are read directly from C++, so downstream tatami-based code can access them without block processing via DelayedArray. Unlike HDF5, Zarr chunks are independent files, so extraction runs in parallel across threads.
